# Gonky

A GUI application for generating custom [Conky](https://github.com/brndnmtthws/conky)
configuration files. Drag and drop system-monitoring components onto a canvas, configure their
properties, and export a ready-to-use `~/.config/conky/conky.conf`.

## Requirements

- **Python 3.10+**
- **GTK 4** — provided by the `python3-gi` system package **or** via pip (see below)
- **Conky** — required only for the live preview feature; the editor itself works without it

## Installation

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/gonky.git
cd gonky
```

### 2. Install system dependencies

Gonky uses GTK 4 via PyGObject. The recommended way is to install the system package:

**Ubuntu / Debian:**
```bash
sudo apt install python3-gi python3-gi-cairo gir1.2-gtk-4.0
```

**Fedora:**
```bash
sudo dnf install python3-gobject gtk4
```

**Arch Linux:**
```bash
sudo pacman -S python-gobject gtk4
```

### 3. Create a virtual environment and install Gonky

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
```

> **Note:** If you installed `python3-gi` as a system package, you may need to create the
> virtual environment with `--system-site-packages` so that PyGObject is accessible:
>
> ```bash
> python3 -m venv --system-site-packages .venv
> source .venv/bin/activate
> pip install -e .
> ```

### 4. (Optional) Install development dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
```

## Running the App

```bash
python -m gonky
```

Or, after `pip install -e .`:

```bash
gonky
```

## Running Tests

```bash
pytest
```

With coverage:

```bash
pytest --cov=gonky --cov-report=term-missing
```

## Project Structure

```
gonky/
├── pyproject.toml          # Build metadata and entry point
├── requirements.txt        # Runtime dependencies
├── requirements-dev.txt    # Development dependencies
├── docs/                   # Technical documentation
├── assets/                 # Icons and CSS stylesheet
├── src/gonky/              # Application source
│   ├── app.py              # Gtk.Application subclass
│   ├── constants.py        # App-wide constants
│   ├── models/             # Data layer (no GTK)
│   ├── logic/              # Business logic (no GTK)
│   ├── ui/                 # GTK widgets and windows
│   └── components/         # Conky component definitions
└── tests/                  # pytest test suite
```

See [`docs/tech-stack.md`](docs/tech-stack.md) for the full technology choice rationale.

